# Generated artefacts are compared byte-for-byte against a fresh generation by
# their `:check` scripts. Without pinning, `core.autocrlf` rewrites them to CRLF
# on Windows checkouts while the generator writes LF, and the check fails on a
# clean tree — a gate that cries wolf is a gate people learn to skip.
packages/contracts/openapi/*.json text eol=lf
packages/contracts/openapi/*.d.ts text eol=lf

# The docs pipeline writes `apps/docs/content/docs/**` with LF on every run, so
# on Windows these show as modified with an EMPTY diff after any `docs:generate`
# — which `lint` runs. That permanent phantom churn is worse than cosmetic: it
# invites a blanket `git checkout -- apps/docs` that silently reverts real edits.
apps/docs/content/docs/** text eol=lf
